Drape is the custom rendering engine for CoMaps.

The main difference from most rendering engines is that it
supports dynamically hiding items based on priorities and space.
This is called displacement.

The drape/ directory contains just the rendering engine;
drape_frontend/ contains things like classes to draw text and icons.

There are three main threads involved:
- BackendRenderer loads map data
- FrontendRenderer organises for rendering to take place
- The platform UI thread renders the rest of the UI that is not part of the map.

Most of the interesting logic (e.g., item visibility) lies on the FrontendRenderer thread.
Data is passed between threads by ThreadCommutator using message_subclasses.

Everything drawn on the map has an overlay. Some overlays are not drawn (if !IsVisible()),
and OverlayTree automatically hides some overlays using SetIsVisible.

Every overlay has an OverlayHandle. Most of the interesting logic is in the OverlayTree.
Notably, OverlayHandles' OverlayIDs are not unique. Related overlays can have the same ID.
